`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{question:"Your release-notes workflow handles routine releases, but some need steps you can't list ahead of time. An agent would publish straight to customers, with no review and no way to pull a note back. What do you do for those releases?",options:[{label:"Move them to the agent, because you can't list the steps",feedback:"Steps you can't list aren't enough, because a wrong step also has to be caught and recovered from."},{label:"Keep the workflow, and send those releases to a person",correct:!0,feedback:"A wrong step can't be caught or recovered from, so stay with the workflow."},{label:"Move them to the agent, and test it once it's live",feedback:"A published note can't be pulled back, so a test after launch catches the mistake too late."}]}),`
